      "summaries": {
        "en": "Telegram Desktop (tdesktop) is the official cross-platform desktop client for Telegram, enabling secure messaging across Windows, macOS, and Linux with full feature parity to mobile apps. Built in C++ for performance, it implements MTProto protocol encryption directly, offering end-to-end encrypted chats and self-destructing messages while maintaining a responsive native interface. Developers can study its clean architecture for multi-platform app design, or modify the open-source code to create custom Telegram clients with specialized features like automated bots or enhanced privacy controls.",
        "zh": "Telegram Desktop（tdesktop）是Telegram官方推出的跨平台桌面客户端，支持Windows、macOS和Linux系统，实现了与移动端完全同步的即时通讯功能。该项目采用C++编写，直接集成了MTProto协议加密层，提供端到端加密聊天和定时销毁消息等安全特性，其原生界面架构保证了低资源占用下的流畅体验。开发者可借鉴其清晰的跨平台代码组织方式，或基于开源代码定制专属客户端，例如添加自动化消息处理机器人或强化隐私管控模块，适合学习现代桌面应用开发与安全通信实践。",
        "es": "Telegram Desktop (tdesktop) is the official cross-platform desktop client for Telegram, enabling secure messaging across Windows, macOS, and Linux with full feature parity to mobile apps. Built in C++ for performance, it implements MTProto protocol encryption directly, offering end-to-end encrypted chats and self-destructing messages while maintaining a responsive native interface. Developers can study its clean architecture for multi-platform app design, or modify the open-source code to create custom Telegram clients with specialized features like automated bots or enhanced privacy controls.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "tdesktop stands out for messenger, multi-platform, and telegram in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Telegram Desktop (tdesktop) is the official cross-platform desktop client for Telegram, enabling secure messaging across Windows, macOS, and Linux with full feature parity to mobile apps. Built in C++ for performance, it implements MTProto protocol encryption directly, offering end-to-end encrypted chats and self-destructing messages while maintaining a responsive native interface. Developers can study its clean architecture for multi-platform app design, or modify the open-source code to create custom Telegram clients with specialized features like automated bots or enhanced privacy controls.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
