      "summaries": {
        "en": "MLX-VLM is an open-source package that enables running and customizing vision-language models directly on Apple Silicon Macs, addressing the need for local AI without cloud dependencies. It leverages Apple's MLX framework to efficiently handle multimodal tasks by unifying image and text processing through optimized GPU acceleration. Developers can use it for local image captioning, visual question answering, or fine-tuning models like LLaVA and Florence-2 for specific applications, making advanced vision-language AI accessible on personal hardware.",
        "zh": "MLX-VLM 是一个开源工具包，专为在 Apple Silicon Mac 上本地运行和微调视觉语言模型而设计，解决了依赖云端服务的限制。它基于苹果的 MLX 框架，通过高效的 GPU 加速统一处理图像和文本，实现多模态任务如图像描述和视觉问答。技术亮点在于利用 MLX 的优化能力，使模型在本地硬件上流畅执行，降低了使用门槛。用户可轻松应用它进行本地图像分析、自定义模型训练，或实验如 LLaVA 等先进模型，为研究和开发提供便捷的本地化 AI 解决方案。",
        "es": "MLX-VLM is an open-source package that enables running and customizing vision-language models directly on Apple Silicon Macs, addressing the need for local AI without cloud dependencies. It leverages Apple's MLX framework to efficiently handle multimodal tasks by unifying image and text processing through optimized GPU acceleration. Developers can use it for local image captioning, visual question answering, or fine-tuning models like LLaVA and Florence-2 for specific applications, making advanced vision-language AI accessible on personal hardware.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "mlx-vlm stands out for apple-silicon, florence2, and idefics in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "MLX-VLM is an open-source package that enables running and customizing vision-language models directly on Apple Silicon Macs, addressing the need for local AI without cloud dependencies. It leverages Apple's MLX framework to efficiently handle multimodal tasks by unifying image and text processing through optimized GPU acceleration. Developers can use it for local image captioning, visual question answering, or fine-tuning models like LLaVA and Florence-2 for specific applications, making advanced vision-language AI accessible on personal hardware.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-vlm for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
